 The BFD 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Brendan Lynch/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 KKR has agreed to a $250 million settlement with the U.S. Justice Department , over its alleged failure to file proper pre-merger notifications on over a dozen deals in 2021 and 2022.

 Why it's the BFD: This is the largest civil penalty ever for HSR Act violations.

 Yes, but: KKR may be smarting from the headlines, but not from the actual settlement.

 All of the $250 million will be reimbursed by outside law firms, none of which KKR is publicly identifying. It won't be required to have its co-CEOs sign future pre-merger notification filings — something DOJ floated but which KKR had strongly opposed. Finally, DOJ originally wanted $650 million. The bottom line: This settles all litigation and ongoing investigations between the two sides, including a countersuit filed by KKR, and doesn't create any new legal precedents for other PE firms.

 
 
